Multithreading - 
	Multithreading is the ability of a process to execute multiple threads concurrently within the same process.
	
Benefits of Multithreading
	1. Improved Responsiveness
		A user can continue interacting with the application while background work is running.
	2. Better CPU Utilization
		Modern CPUs have multiple cores.
	3. Faster Execution
		Tasks can run concurrently.
	4. Resource Sharing
		Threads share:
			Memory
			Files
			Code
		No expensive IPC is needed.
Is Multithreading Always Good?
	No.

	It introduces problems such as:
		Race Conditions
		Deadlocks
		Starvation
		Synchronization Issues
		
Multithreading is the execution of multiple threads within the same process. Since threads share the process's memory and resources, they are lightweight and efficient. Multithreading improves responsiveness, CPU utilization, throughput, and resource sharing. Common real-world examples include web browsers, video streaming applications, web servers, online games, and IDEs, where different threads handle separate tasks concurrently.

